  "challenge": "Video production at scale hits a hard bottleneck \u2014 manual editing. Each video requires a skilled editor spending hours on assembly, transitions, text overlays, and export. When content demand calls for dozens of videos per week, the traditional approach simply doesn't scale without proportionally scaling expensive editor headcount.",
  "approach": "Replaced the manual editing workflow with an API-driven production pipeline. Video templates define structure, transitions, and brand elements programmatically. Source assets are assembled through API calls to video rendering services. The system handles text overlay personalization, audio sync, format optimization, and multi-platform export \u2014 all without opening an editing application.",
  "result": "Production throughput increased 10x while reducing per-video cost dramatically. The API-driven approach eliminated the editing bottleneck entirely \u2014 videos are produced programmatically from templates and assets. The system handles format variations for different platforms automatically, meaning one piece of source content generates multiple platform-optimized outputs.",
